By the way, I think the only debatable point in all those sections is 
the cmavo {ne'a}, which has two popular meanings/uses. Those meanings 
are {fi'o se zvajbi} i.e. "near/in the vicinity of", and {fi'o se mlana} 
"on the side of". The former is compatible with the latter, but not 
vice-versa.

